    {
      "ancestors": [],
      "attributes": [
        {
          "doc_text": " An iterator whose items are random-accessible efficiently",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            15831,
            15892
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": "",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            15893,
            15896
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " # Safety",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            15897,
            15909
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": "",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            15910,
            15913
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " The iterator's `size_hint` must be exact and cheap to call.",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            15914,
            15977
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": "",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            15978,
            15981
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " `TrustedRandomAccessNoCoerce::size` may not be overridden.",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            15982,
            16044
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": "",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            16045,
            16048
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " All subtypes and all supertypes of `Self` must also implement `TrustedRandomAccess`.",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            16049,
            16137
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " In particular, this means that types with non-invariant parameters usually can not have",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            16138,
            16229
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " an impl for `TrustedRandomAccess` that depends on any trait bounds on such parameters, except",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            16230,
            16327
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " for bounds that come from the respective struct/enum definition itself, or bounds involving",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            16328,
            16423
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " traits that themselves come with a guarantee similar to this one.",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            16424,
            16493
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": "",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            16494,
            16497
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " If `Self: ExactSizeIterator` then `self.len()` must always produce results consistent",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            16498,
            16587
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " with `self.size()`.",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            16588,
            16611
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": "",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            16612,
            16615
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " If `Self: Iterator`, then `<Self as Iterator>::__iterator_get_unchecked(&mut self, idx)`",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            16616,
            16708
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " must be safe to call provided the following conditions are met.",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            16709,
            16776
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": "",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            16777,
            16780
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " 1. `0 <= idx` and `idx < self.size()`.",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            16781,
            16823
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " 2. If `Self: !Clone`, then `self.__iterator_get_unchecked(idx)` is never called with the same",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            16824,
            16921
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": "    index on `self` more than once.",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            16922,
            16960
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " 3. After `self.__iterator_get_unchecked(idx)` has been called, then `self.next_back()` will",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            16961,
            17056
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": "    only be called at most `self.size() - idx - 1` times. If `Self: Clone` and `self` is cloned,",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            17057,
            17156
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": "    then this number is calculated for `self` and its clone individually,",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            17157,
            17233
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": "    but `self.next_back()` calls that happened before the cloning count for both `self` and the clone.",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            17234,
            17339
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " 4. After `self.__iterator_get_unchecked(idx)` has been called, then only the following methods",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            17340,
            17438
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": "    will be called on `self` or on any new clones of `self`:",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            17439,
            17502
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": "     * `std::clone::Clone::clone`",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            17503,
            17539
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": "     * `std::iter::Iterator::size_hint`",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            17540,
            17582
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": "     * `std::iter::DoubleEndedIterator::next_back`",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            17583,
            17636
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": "     * `std::iter::ExactSizeIterator::len`",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            17637,
            17682
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": "     * `std::iter::Iterator::__iterator_get_unchecked`",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            17683,
            17740
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": "     * `std::iter::TrustedRandomAccessNoCoerce::size`",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            17741,
            17797
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " 5. If `Self` is a subtype of `T`, then `self` is allowed to be coerced",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            17798,
            17872
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": "    to `T`. If `self` is coerced to `T` after `self.__iterator_get_unchecked(idx)` has already",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            17873,
            17970
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": "    been called, then no methods except for the ones listed under 4. are allowed to be called",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            17971,
            18067
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": "    on the resulting value of type `T`, either. Multiple such coercion steps are allowed.",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            18068,
            18160
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": "    Regarding 2. and 3., the number of times `__iterator_get_unchecked(idx)` or `next_back()` is",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            18161,
            18260
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": "    called on `self` and the resulting value of type `T` (and on further coercion results with",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            18261,
            18358
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": "    super-supertypes) are added together and their sums must not exceed the specified bounds.",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            18359,
            18455
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": "",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            18456,
            18459
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " Further, given that these conditions are met, it must guarantee that:",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            18460,
            18533
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": "",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            18534,
            18537
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " * It does not change the value returned from `size_hint`",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            18538,
            18598
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " * It must be safe to call the methods listed above on `self` after calling",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            18599,
            18677
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": "   `self.__iterator_get_unchecked(idx)`, assuming that the required traits are implemented.",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            18678,
            18772
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " * It must also be safe to drop `self` after calling `self.__iterator_get_unchecked(idx)`.",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            18773,
            18866
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " * If `Self` is a subtype of `T`, then it must be safe to coerce `self` to `T`.",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            18867,
            18949
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": null,
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            19110,
            19124
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": null,
          "path": "unstable",
          "range": [
            19125,
            19187
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": null,
          "path": "rustc_specialization_trait",
          "range": [
            19188,
            19217
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        }
      ],
